{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A containerized web application runs on node1 as the unprivileged appsvc account and serves HTTP on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Post-reboot evidence shows Podman operating rootlessly, the nginx container running with port 8080 mapped to port 80, HTTP 200 with the expected content, and the container monitor owned by appsvc. The account uses /sbin/nologin and had zero active login sessions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4ae2e0e071fd4483","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The application starts automatically at boot without requiring an active appsvc login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy pre-restart service was observed, the node acknowledged a reboot, its boot ID changed, and the recovered system immediately showed the OpenRC service enabled and started, HTTP responding, the rootless container running, and no appsvc login session.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e202744b8fd44a5f","cmd-2229a80ac690483c","cmd-2a4d513a52814b80","cmd-4ae2e0e071fd4483","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The installation, account setup, subordinate mappings, cgroup configuration, service construction, corrective troubleshooting, and two bounded reboot tests all had clear roles in delivering or validating the requested outcome. Package health remained unchanged apart from the pre-existing chrony drift entry. Three low-risk temporary artifacts were unnecessarily retained: /tmp/appsvc-web-body from a service check, /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log from the first reboot, and /tmp/[REDACTED].log from the final reboot. They remained present in the final snapshot rather than being cleaned up. No broader damage, failed package state, conflicting listener, or unnecessary security weakening was demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b510339d3b0f45c8","cmd-fbb731950f69491e","cmd-2229a80ac690483c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct post-reboot observations establish a rootless appsvc-owned container serving HTTP successfully on port 8080 and starting through OpenRC with no active appsvc login session. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered service and content. Only minor retained temporary evidence files reduce operational hygiene.","limitations":["The generic lifecycle failed-services probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on an Alpine/OpenRC node; final service health therefore relies primarily on direct executor observations.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory is bounded and does not constitute a complete filesystem residue audit."]}
